cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "APEX — Automated Photometry EXtraction"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
# NOTE: replace the entity author below with your real name / ORCID for
# academic citation (e.g. family-names / given-names / orcid).
authors:
  - name: "The APEX Project"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-06-20"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Diu1773/APEX_AutomatedPhotometryEXtraction"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - photometry
  - aperture-photometry
  - PSF-photometry
  - light-curves
  - color-magnitude-diagram
  - isochrone
  - astronomy
  - FITS
abstract: >-
  APEX is a desktop and headless Python pipeline for astronomical aperture and
  PSF photometry, covering source detection, WCS plate solving, forced
  photometry, color-magnitude diagrams with PARSEC isochrone fitting, and
  multi-night differential light curves with period analysis.
